<%# Create, on the shared record-page shell: one column, one heading, the form in a Details section.

    Measured at 1366px before this, on the input rather than the wrapper: this form's fields were 1020px
    wide while the record page it leads to is 726px, because the page had no column of its own and inherited
    the layout's `max-w-7xl`. Five different form measures existed across the app - 384, 630, 726, 854 and
    1020px of field - and a form's measure should not change between creating a record and editing it.

    The shell is `admin/shared/_record_page`, the same partial the record page uses, so the two cannot drift:
    a create page is that page with no lifecycle actions and one section. %>
<%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_page",
           locals: { title: "New teacher", breadcrumbs: @breadcrumbs } do %>
  <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section",
             locals: { title: "Details", hint: "Saved when you press Create teacher." } do %>
    <%= render "form", teacher: @teacher %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
